course: dictionary
lesson: 15680
title: Tied: many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Tied» is a good example. Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits. «She tied her shoelaces before the race.» Tied here is the past form of tie, so she fixed her laces with a knot.
explain: «The score was tied at 10 all.» Here tied means both teams have the same score. Nobody is winning. The words «score» and «10 all» are the clues. In maths, you can also use tied when you share things into equal groups, like «twenty pencils, tied in groups of 5».
explain: «Maya was tied up with homework all weekend.» Tied up means busy, with no free time. Notice that tied up here is not about rope at all. Always ask: which meaning fits the sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Tied is the past form of tie, as in «she tied a knot».
fact: «Tied» can mean fixed with string or rope, as in «he tied the parcel».
fact: «Tied» can mean having the same score as another team or player.
fact: «Tied up» means busy, or not free to use, as in «my money is tied up».
fact: «Tongue-tied» means too shy or nervous to speak.
exercise: «She tied her shoelaces before the race.» What does tied mean here? | Lost in the race | Busy with work | *Fixed with a knot | Had the same score
exercise: «The score was tied at 10 all.» What does tied mean here? | Won the game by a lot | Very tired | *Both teams have the same score | Fixed with string
exercise: Twenty pencils are «tied in groups of 5». How many groups are there? | 15 | *4 | 25 | 5
test: «Maya was tied up with homework all weekend.» What does tied up mean? | Fixed tightly with rope | Happy and relaxed | Fast asleep | *Busy, with no free time
test: Which word is the past form of the verb tie? | tying | ties | *tied | tie
exam: «At the end of the match, Ben's team and Sam's team are tied.» What does tied mean? | The match was cancelled | Ben's team has won the match | *Both teams have the same score | Sam's team has lost their ball
